  ('1036353084576076821', 'Mona Lisa Smile', 2003, 'Drama, History, Romance', 'Mike Newell, Anastas N. Michos, Paul Schiff', 'Lawrence Konner, Mark Rosenthal', 'Julia Roberts, Kirsten Dunst, Julia Stiles, Maggie Gyllenhaal, Ginnifer Goodwin, Dominic West, Juliet Stevenson, Marcia Gay Harden', 'PG-13', 'Katherine Watson is a recent UCLA graduate hired to teach art history at the prestigious all-female Wellesley College, in 1953. Determined to confront the outdated mores of society and the institution that embraces them, Katherine inspires her traditional students, including Betty and Joan, to challenge the lives they are expected to lead.', 'Katherine Watson is a recent UCLA graduate hired to teach art history at the prestigious all-female Wellesley College, in 1953. Determined to confront the outdated mores of society and the institution that embraces them, Katherine inspires her traditional students, including Betty and Joan, to challenge the lives they are expected to lead.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/bg0VKsXnLjIZ0cHmZHZLs9gzrvm.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:11820'),
  ('696996831365254926', 'Monaco Forever', 1984, 'Comedy', 'William A. Levey, Daryn Okada', 'C. William Pitt, William A. Levey', 'Charles Pitt, Martha Ferris, Jean-Claude Van Damme, Sydney Lassick, Michelle Bauer, Clement von Franckenstein, Shawn Southwick, Danièle Romer', 'NR', 'An American jewel thief in Monaco encounters various characters while trying to set up a robbery.', 'An American jewel thief in Monaco encounters various characters while trying to set up a robbery.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/t1oU3442hRaW8XQLqlK9R1HIxRB.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:76172'),
  ('288103152099415226', 'Monday', 2000, 'Comedy, Crime, Mystery, Thriller', 'Shojiro Urahama, SABU, Kazuto Sato', 'SABU', 'Shinichi Tsutsumi, Yasuko Matsuyuki, Nanako Okochi, Naomi Nishida, Masanobu Ando, Ren Osugi, Hijiri Kojima, Akaji Maro', null, 'A simple funeral turns a man''s world Topsy turvy. He wakes up in a posh hotel room, totally clueless about how he got there. Slowly, he recalls what happened a day before.', 'A simple funeral turns a man''s world Topsy turvy. He wakes up in a posh hotel room, totally clueless about how he got there. Slowly, he recalls what happened a day before.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/ha06SfVtGPaRdMuBxe9IcPo8SzY.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:36246'),
  ('221365106703343588', 'Monday', 2021, 'Drama, Romance', 'Stavros Liokalos, Argyris Papadimitropoulos, Christos Karamanis', 'Argyris Papadimitropoulos, Rob Hayes', 'Sebastian Stan, Denise Gough, Dominique Tipper, Vangelis Mourikis, Yorgos Pirpassopoulos, Elli Tringou, Marissa Triantafyllidou, Syllas Tzoumerkas', 'R', 'A spark on a Friday can lead to a sizzling weekend fling, but what happens when you get to the inevitable Monday?', 'A spark on a Friday can lead to a sizzling weekend fling, but what happens when you get to the inevitable Monday?', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/o4Gc5quiCBtiW6mgkPvDWKAiFVs.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:550524'),
  ('539415523202418278', 'Monday Morning', 2002, 'Drama, Comedy, Romance', 'Otar Iosseliani, William Lubtchansky', 'Otar Iosseliani', 'Jacques Bidou, Anne Kravz-Tarnavsky, Narda Blanchet, Dato Tarielachvili, Yannick Carpentier, Jérémy Rochigneux, Amiran Amiranashvili (II), Pascal Aubier', null, 'Vincent lives in a village, along the Rhône. Every morning he goes to the factory to work, and in the evening he takes care of his family. One day, he decides to go on a trip with the money given by his father.', 'Vincent lives in a village, along the Rhône. Every morning he goes to the factory to work, and in the evening he takes care of his family. One day, he decides to go on a trip with the money given by his father.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/fli9wdNEWksXZlSfyxaOa1mF23.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:49696'),
  ('124681833521296626', 'Mondays in the Sun', 2002, 'Drama, Comedy', 'Fernando León de Aranoa, Alfredo Mayo, Antonio Ordóñez', 'Fernando León de Aranoa, Ignacio del Moral', 'Javier Bardem, Luis Tosar, José Ángel Egido, Nieve de Medina, Enrique Villén, Celso Bugallo, Laura Domínguez, Aida Folch', null, 'After the closure of their shipyard in Northern Spain, a few former workers: Santa, José, Lino, Amador, Sergei and Reina keep in touch. They meet mainly at a bar owned by their former colleague Rico. Santa is the most superficially confident and unofficial leader of the group. A court case hangs over him relating to a shipyard lamp he smashed during a protest against the closure. José is bitter that his wife, Ana, is employed when he is not.', 'After the closure of their shipyard in Northern Spain, a few former workers: Santa, José, Lino, Amador, Sergei and Reina keep in touch. They meet mainly at a bar owned by their former colleague Rico. Santa is the most superficially confident and unofficial leader of the group. A court case hangs over him relating to a shipyard lamp he smashed during a protest against the closure. José is bitter that his wife, Ana, is employed when he is not.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/4BlI5weSiYUU1YnjqdaPLnOzc3Z.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:54580'),
  ('29826638992083216', 'Mondo', 1995, 'Drama', 'Tony Gatlif', 'Tony Gatlif', 'Ovidiu Balan, Philippe Petit, Pierrette Fesch, Schahla Aalam, Maurice Maurin, Maurice Maurin, Maurice Maurin, Catherine Brun', null, 'Mondo, a young orphaned gypsy, finds himself in France, where he scouts out potential foster families, evades the police and meets an assortment of eccentric people. In his travels, Mondo first encounters a magician who takes on the boy as an assistant. Then he moves on again, eventually befriending Dadi, a street-smart vagrant, and Giordan, a wise fisherman. All the while, the boy keeps an eye out for would-be parents.', 'Mondo, a young orphaned gypsy, finds himself in France, where he scouts out potential foster families, evades the police and meets an assortment of eccentric people. In his travels, Mondo first encounters a magician who takes on the boy as an assistant. Then he moves on again, eventually befriending Dadi, a street-smart vagrant, and Giordan, a wise fisherman. All the while, the boy keeps an eye out for would-be parents.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/fVbwUY29Qs1Sx6Bwn2KYxzyxSEd.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:124834'),
  ('507465465105999918', 'Mondo candido', 1975, 'Adventure, Comedy', 'Gualtiero Jacopetti, Franco Prosperi', 'Gualtiero Jacopetti', 'Christopher Brown, Michele Miller, Jacques Herlin, Steffen Zacharias, Gianfranco D''Angelo, Salvatore Baccaro, Alessandro Haber, José Quaglio', null, 'Voltaire, a 16th century author was furious that learned members of a "civilized" society could claim that the apparent senseless violence and mayhem wrought by disasters, war, disease, man''s cruelty, etc. was actually only a part of some ''greater good''. After all, God (being perfect) could not ''logically'' have created anything but the ''best of all possible'' universes.', 'Voltaire, a 16th century author was furious that learned members of a "civilized" society could claim that the apparent senseless violence and mayhem wrought by disasters, war, disease, man''s cruelty, etc. was actually only a part of some ''greater good''. After all, God (being perfect) could not ''logically'' have created anything but the ''best of all possible'' universes.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/rKqVVcmfAbOE2IkEziIWlwavH1r.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:74645'),
  ('189146978272934704', 'Mondo Cane', 1962, 'Documentary', 'Paolo Cavara, Gualtiero Jacopetti, Franco Prosperi', 'Gualtiero Jacopetti, Paolo Cavara', 'Rossano Brazzi, Stefano Sibaldi', null, 'A documentary consisting of a series of travelogue vignettes providing glimpses into cultural practices throughout the world intended to shock or surprise, including an insect banquet and a memorable look at a practicing South Pacific cargo cult.', 'A documentary consisting of a series of travelogue vignettes providing glimpses into cultural practices throughout the world intended to shock or surprise, including an insect banquet and a memorable look at a practicing South Pacific cargo cult.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/kw8MBBknqE0GO7JuP7F3QDIHLt9.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:32688'),
  ('389886008696131948', 'Mondo Cane 2', 1963, 'Documentary, Horror', 'Gualtiero Jacopetti, Franco Prosperi, Benito Frattari', 'Franco Prosperi, Gualtiero Jacopetti', 'Arnaldo Caivano, Gualtiero Jacopetti', null, 'The official sequel to the original shockumentary, presenting new and bizarre behavior from around the world, including cruelty, graphic gore, and strange rituals.', 'The official sequel to the original shockumentary, presenting new and bizarre behavior from around the world, including cruelty, graphic gore, and strange rituals.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/sHWqahepue7O2HMQImMRCAyc3uh.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:87524'),
  ('646891582241274559', 'Mondo Freudo', 1966, 'Documentary', 'Lee Frost', null, 'Judy Adler, Carol Baughman, Baby Bubbles, Bob Cresse, James E. McLarty, Coleen O''Brien, Margo Lynn Sweet, Charlotte', null, 'A “hidden camera” takes the viewer on a worldwide tour of sexual practices and rituals, including Tijuana strippers, Asian sex shows, British prostitutes, New York devil worshipers and a Mexican slave market.', 'A “hidden camera” takes the viewer on a worldwide tour of sexual practices and rituals, including Tijuana strippers, Asian sex shows, British prostitutes, New York devil worshipers and a Mexican slave market.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/aWUUZL0dFhu6s7IFeUMvqTSQpxJ.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:91482'),
  ('924665061303419400', 'Mondo New York', 1988, 'Documentary', 'Harvey Keith, Leonard Wong', 'Harvey Keith, David Silver', 'Joey Arias, Rick Aviles, Joe Coleman, Emilio Cubeiro, Karen Finley, Dean Johnson, Phoebe Legere, Lydia Lunch', 'R', 'A young woman wanders around New York City and stumbles across a number of strange characters and settings that represent the "underground" areas of the city. She sees stand up comedy in Central Park, a prostitution auction, a voodoo ceremony, an S&M club, and a number of very interesting performance artists. These are just a few of the sights and sounds of New York that she encounters.', 'A young woman wanders around New York City and stumbles across a number of strange characters and settings that represent the "underground" areas of the city. She sees stand up comedy in Central Park, a prostitution auction, a voodoo ceremony, an S&M club, and a number of very interesting performance artists. These are just a few of the sights and sounds of New York that she encounters.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/z7Z3yyplquKaxd4o92eJUvaOWCr.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:41964'),
  ('267874970095251611', 'Mondo Topless', 1966, 'Documentary', 'Russ Meyer, Russ Meyer', 'Russ Meyer', 'Babette Bardot, Pat Barrington, Sin Lenee, Darlene Grey, Diane Young, Darla Paris, Trina Lamar, Veronique Gabriel', null, 'Completely topless. Completely uninhibited. The craze that began in San Francisco is now exploding across the USA and Europe.', 'Completely topless. Completely uninhibited. The craze that began in San Francisco is now exploding across the USA and Europe.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/vpudwaFJJA9nE6p80ZQLE3qKHpc.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:5726'),
  ('120793748640163076', 'Mondo Trasho', 1969, 'Comedy, Crime', 'John Waters, John Waters', 'John Waters', 'Mary Vivian Pearce, Divine, David Lochary, Mink Stole, Bob Skidmore, Margie Skidmore, Berenica Cipcus, Jack Walsh', null, 'A day in the lives of a hit-and-run driver and her victim, and the bizarre things that happen to them before and after they collide (sexual assault by a crazed foot-fetishist, visions of the Virgin Mary, strange chicken-foot grafting operations).', 'A day in the lives of a hit-and-run driver and her victim, and the bizarre things that happen to them before and after they collide (sexual assault by a crazed foot-fetishist, visions of the Virgin Mary, strange chicken-foot grafting operations).', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/yxMYVGGnX4lo8S5zYfZpCDWtnte.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:30645'),
  ('567162655325103945', 'Mondo Weirdo', 1990, 'Drama, Horror, Mystery, Fantasy', 'Carl Andersen', 'Carl Andersen', 'Soledad Marceignac, Frank Khunne, David Hollman, Jessica F. Manera, Modell D''oo, Ron Lourid, Barbara Bourbon, Tommy Simon', null, 'A young girl embarks on a trip to paranoia paradise.', 'A young girl embarks on a trip to paranoia paradise.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/oPh9BpIaDn6UQZYYqzXxkasB4Z7.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:181601'),
  ('1121932188975537183', 'Mondocane', 2021, 'Action, Crime, Science Fiction, Drama', 'Alessandro Celli, Giuseppe Maio', 'Alessandro Celli, Antonio Leotti', 'Alessandro Borghi, Dennis Protopapa, Giuliano Soprano, Barbara Ronchi, Josafat Vagni, Federica Torchetti, Ludovica Nasti, Lavinia Novelli', null, 'In the near future, the southern Italian city of Taranto is surrounded by barbed wire that no one, not even the police, dares to cross. The poorest are left fighting for survival, while gangs compete for the territory. Two thirteen-year-old orphans who grew up together, dream of joining one of the gangs.', 'In the near future, the southern Italian city of Taranto is surrounded by barbed wire that no one, not even the police, dares to cross. The poorest are left fighting for survival, while gangs compete for the territory. Two thirteen-year-old orphans who grew up together, dream of joining one of the gangs.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/gOuJBz9u1YVWwvx12lJX56yUT6I.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:744278'),
